NAME
       wrsadc - boundary layer for resonance-safe dispatch and structural
                awareness in TriadicFrameworks

SYNOPSIS
       wrsadc_shell.sh
       wrsadc_core.py

DESCRIPTION
       WRSADC (Wave-Resonance Structural-Awareness Dispatch Core) is the
       boundary layer that mediates between external actions and RTT-Inside
       computation. It ensures that all operations entering the Engine are:

           • boundary-safe
           • resonance-aligned
           • lineage-tracked
           • structurally aware

       WRSADC does not perform domain logic. It enforces the rules that make
       domain logic safe to execute.

COMPONENTS
       wrsadc_shell.sh
              Outer membrane. Initializes environment, state, and logging.
              Provides safe entry points for shell-level operations.

       wrsadc_core.py
              Inner interpreter. Performs structural-awareness checks,
              lineage updates, and safe dispatch of user-defined functions.

       3pack integration
              WRSADC uses the 3-Pack primitives (P1, P2, P3) to structure
              every action into a begin → transform → close cycle.

FEATURES
       Boundary Safety
              Ensures that all incoming operations conform to RTT-aligned
              structural constraints.

       Structural Awareness
              Injects metadata describing context, lineage, and resonance
              state into each dispatch.

       Safe Dispatch
              Executes user-defined functions through a controlled interface
              that prevents unsafe transitions.

       Lineage Tracking
              Records the triadic history of operations for reproducibility
              and interpretability.

USAGE
       Shell entry:
              ./wrsadc_shell.sh

       Python entry:
              from wrsadc_core import WRSADCCore
              core = WRSADCCore()
              core.dispatch(fn)

       Combined with 3-Pack:
              primitive1.sh
              core.dispatch(step)
              primitive3.sh

WORKFLOW
       1. Shell initializes WRSADC environment.
       2. User invokes an operation (shell or Python).
       3. WRSADC applies structural-awareness checks.
       4. WRSADC wraps the operation in a triadic cycle.
       5. WRSADC dispatches the operation safely.
       6. Lineage and state are updated.

WHEN TO USE WRSADC
       • When executing any operation that crosses a boundary.
       • When structural-awareness metadata is required.
       • When dispatch must be safe, reversible, or lineage-tracked.
       • When integrating with the 3-Pack or RTT-Inside Engine.

FILES
       wrsadc_shell.sh
              Shell interface and environment setup.

       wrsadc_core.py
              Python interpreter and dispatch engine.

       3pak-shell/
              Provides triadic primitives and state/logging infrastructure.

NOTES
       WRSADC is not a business-logic engine. It is a membrane. All domain
       logic lives inside the Engine. WRSADC ensures that only safe, aligned,
       triad-structured actions reach it.

